WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.500
We're here to take a quick look at the Amazon Tax Exemption Program.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:17.080
After watching this video, you'll understand what the Amazon Tax Exemption Program is,

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:22.440
how to enroll, and how to get exemption certificates for your tax exempt sales.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:27.960
The Amazon Tax Exemption Program, or ATEP, can make selling to tax exempt buyers a little

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:28.403
easier.

00:00:28.403 --> 00:00:34.160
ATEP automates the process, applying applicable tax exemptions at the time of sale,

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.560
so you don't have to process a refund after the fact.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:42.600
When a buyer makes a tax exempt purchase from a seller enrolled in ATEP, ATEP populates

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.520
the exemption certificate with the seller's legal entity name and the buyer's exemption

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:48.029
information.

00:00:48.029 --> 00:00:53.120
Amazon then automatically processes the tax exemption for the sale.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:59.440
ATEP also stores exemption certificates for tax exempt sales for future reference.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:04.200
You can enroll in ATEP from your seller account by clicking the "Tax Settings" link under

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.369
the "Settings" drop-down menu.

00:01:06.369 --> 00:01:09.840
From the "Tax Settings" page, click "View edit

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:15.800
your tax collection, obligations, and shipping and handling and gift wrap tax settings.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:20.120
Here you can update your tax calculation settings to enroll in ATEP.

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:21.920
Note that there may still

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:28.720
be special cases where you'll need to execute a post-order refund such as non-ATEP FBA exempt

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.816
customers or freight forwarders.

00:01:30.816 --> 00:01:33.960
Getting tax exemption certificates is easy

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.893
once you've enrolled in ATEP.

00:01:35.893 --> 00:01:39.760
From your seller account, select the "Reports" tab, then "Tax

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:45.880
Document Library." Next, select the "Tax Exemption Certificates" tab.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:50.200
Select either "Order ID" or "Date Range" to sort.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:55.640
Once you've entered your search criteria, click "Get Report" to submit your request.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:00.400
Keep in mind that certificates become available 48 hours after you have confirmed shipment

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.360
of your tax exempt order.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:06.046
That does it for the Amazon Tax Exemption Program.

00:02:06.046 --> 00:02:07.240
Thanks for tuning in.
